  "title": "How Many: mono-, uni-, di- and poly-",
  "short": "Number prefixes come in Greek and Latin pairs: mono- and uni- (one), di- and bi- (two), poly- and multi- (many).",
  "trouble": "Learners mix the Greek and Latin sets; both are right in their own words (monorail, unicycle).",
