  "practice": null,
  "lesson": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "t": "p",
        "html": "Numbers come in pairs of prefixes, one Greek and one Latin. A <i>monorail</i> (Greek) and a <i>unicycle</i> (Latin) each have one of something. A <i>dilemma</i> (Greek) is a choice between two, and a <i>bicycle</i> (Latin) has two wheels. A <i>polygon</i> (Greek) has many sides, and to <i>multiply</i> (Latin) is to make many."
      },
      {
