        "cap": "A girl holds one balloon, labeled mono, and a boy holds a bunch of balloons, labeled poly."
      },
      {
        "t": "key",
        "html": "<b>One</b>: <b>mono-</b> (Greek), <b>uni-</b> (Latin). <b>Two</b>: <b>di-</b> (Greek), <b>bi-</b> (Latin). <b>Many</b>: <b>poly-</b> (Greek), <b>multi-</b> (Latin)."
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "html": "The list has fewer number words than you might expect, but each is a good one. A <b>unanimous</b> vote comes from one mind (<i>un-</i> + <i>anim</i>, mind). A <b>monotonous</b> voice stays on one tone. A <b>dichotomy</b> cuts something in two. A <b>polymath</b> has learned many subjects."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "The parts and their words"
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-roots",
        "opts": {
          "max": 10,
          "roots": [
            "mono",
            "uni"
          ]
        },
        "cap": "mono- and uni- (one)."
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-roots",
        "opts": {
          "max": 10,
          "roots": [
            "di",
            "poly"
          ]
        },
        "cap": "di- (two) and poly- (many)."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "Words taken apart"
      },
      {
        "t": "table",
        "head": [
          "Word and meaning",
          "Parts, and what they say"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "<b>monotonous</b><br>dull because it never varies",
            "<b>mono-</b> <i>one</i> + ton <i>tone</i> + -ous<br>→ “of one tone”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>unanimous</b><br>fully agreed by everyone",
            "<b>un</b> <i>one</i> + anim <i>mind</i> + -ous<br>→ “of one mind”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>universal</b><br>applying to all",
            "<b>uni-</b> <i>one</i> + vers <i>turned</i> + -al<br>→ “turned into one (all together)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>dichotomy</b><br>a division into two opposite parts",
            "<b>dicho</b> <i>in two</i> + tom <i>cut</i> + -y<br>→ “a cutting in two”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>polymath</b><br>a person with expert knowledge of many subjects",
            "<b>poly-</b> <i>many</i> + math <i>learning</i><br>→ “one of much learning”"
          ],
          [
            "<b><i>monologue</i></b><br>a long speech by one person",
            "<b>mono-</b> <i>one</i> + log <i>speech</i><br>→ “one person’s speech”"
          ],
          [
            "<b><i>unicycle</i></b><br>a cycle with one wheel",
            "<b>uni-</b> <i>one</i> + cycle <i>wheel</i><br>→ “one wheel”"
          ],
          [
            "<b><i>polygon</i></b><br>a flat shape with many straight sides",
            "<b>poly-</b> <i>many</i> + gon <i>angle</i><br>→ “many angles”"
          ]
        ],
        "cap": "Each word, what it means now, and its parts. Words in italics are familiar words that are not on the list."
      },
      {
        "t": "ex",
        "title": "Use the parts",
        "q": "The vote to name the class turtle Pickles was <b>unanimous</b>. How many students voted against it?",
        "steps": [
          "Take it apart: <b>un</b> (one, from <i>uni-</i>) + <b>anim</b> (mind, as in <i>animate</i>) + <b>-ous</b>.",
          "Literally: “of one mind.”",
          "If everyone is of one mind, no one disagreed."
        ],
        "a": "None: everyone agreed."
      },
