        "t": "mistake",
        "html": "Mixing the Greek and Latin sets, or thinking one is wrong. Both are right in their own words: <i>monorail</i> (Greek) and <i>unicycle</i> (Latin); <i>dilemma</i> (Greek) and <i>bicycle</i> (Latin). Usually a Greek number joins a Greek root and a Latin number joins a Latin root."
